The change belongs in `Scenario.prepare_training_step` in `reef/scenario/scenario.py`. Its early `return None` (lines 350-357) makes every training step wait until the selected artifact serves. That guard needs to apply only in automatic mode.

I didn't write the change or check the trainer code. That code may also need a look, but I'm not confident enough to list it.

{"files": ["reef/scenario/scenario.py"]}

The listing is built from `SampleStore.stored_sample`, which calls `self.data.task_path(item)` for every task. That is probably what reads or materializes the task files. The fix would stop the listing from building full samples. It would use only the item's id, split, digest and train counts.

`reef/service/tasks.py` and `Dispatcher.imported_tasks` are the other places that would change, because `list_imported_tasks` consumes `StoredSample`. I did not open `task_path`, so I'm inferring that it reads the files.

{"files": ["reef/storage/samples.py", "reef/service/tasks.py", "reef/dispatcher/dispatcher.py"]}

The fix belongs in `write_job_data` in `reef/storage/job_data.py`. It builds a list of lines, joins them, and then encodes the result, so the whole file sits in memory three times over. Line 87 does the join and the encode. It should write each line to an open file as it is produced.

I did not make the change.

{"files": ["reef/storage/job_data.py"]}

